### **VI. MOTOR OUTPUT COMPUTATION WITH SATURATION HANDLING**

#### **VI.1 Differential Thrust Allocation Matrix**

```c
const float thrust_matrix[4][3] = {
    { 1.0, -1.0,  1.0},  // Motor 1 (Front Right)
    { 1.0, -1.0, -1.0},  // Motor 2 (Back Right)
    { 1.0,  1.0, -1.0},  // Motor 3 (Back Left)
    { 1.0,  1.0,  1.0}   // Motor 4 (Front Left)
};

void compute_motor_outputs(float control_input[3], float outputs[4]) {
    float raw_thrust[4] = {0};

    // Matrix multiplication: T = M × u
    for(int m = 0; m < 4; m++) {
        raw_thrust[m] = 0;
        for(int c = 0; c < 3; c++) {
            raw_thrust[m] += thrust_matrix[m][c] * control_input[c];
        }
    }

    // Add collective thrust offset
    float thrust_c = 0.5f;  // 50% base throttle
    for(int m = 0; m < 4; m++) {
        raw_thrust[m] += thrust_c;
        outputs[m] = constrain(raw_thrust[m], 1000.0f, 2000.0f);  // PWM range
    }
}
```

**Saturation Handling via Anti-Windup:**
```c
float integral_gain_saturation(float error_sum, float max_integral) {
    if(fabs(error_sum) > max_integral) {
        return copysign(max_integral, error_sum);
    }
    return error_sum;
}
